  "final_message": "Implemented all three versions:\n\n- [Rust](rust/src/main.rs) uses threads and wrapping integer arithmetic.\n- [Plain Python](plain.py) uses worker processes and an inlined SplitMix64 loop.\n- [NumPy Python](fast.py) generates random numbers and processes wall-free blocks in arrays, falling back to individual steps for blocks that cross a wall.\n\nEach version partitions walkers among workers and combines their results with the required tie-break. All three pass **s1a, s1b, s2, and s3** with 1, 4, and 8 workers. The NumPy and plain Python implementations also matched on 250 randomized cases.",
